{"actKind": "new", "audit": {"coverageKind": "newTaxa", "state": "unaudited"}, "id": "2008_zhao.y.l_parsley_peng.j:0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/0:act", "kind": "act", "path": "0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/0", "printedAttribution": "as-record", "source": "2008_zhao.y.l_parsley_peng.j", "subject": "globoeocrinus", "tree": "taxonomy"}
{"audit": {"coverageKind": "diagnoses", "state": "unaudited"}, "id": "2008_zhao.y.l_parsley_peng.j:0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/0:diagnosis", "kind": "diagnosis", "path": "0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/0", "printedAttribution": "as-record", "source": "2008_zhao.y.l_parsley_peng.j", "subject": "globoeocrinus", "text": "Gogiids with globose theca, subcircular to slightly pyriform\nin thecal profile, broadly oval in transverse cross section.\nFive to seven, rarely eight, irregular circlets of variously\npolyg onal thecal plates that are commonly, increasingly\ndisrupted by intercalates and sutural pores during ontogeny.\nEmplacement of thecal sutural pores ontogenetically ranges from\nnone, to pores at distal ends of plates under transverse\nambulacral grooves, to pores over entire theca or with\na probable posterior patch of non-pored plates, to large\nwell-formed pores on all thecal plates on large mature specimens.\nPores just distal to food grooves unusually large and acquire\nmature morephology by late juvenile stage. Periproct protruding\nvertically from bulged posterior side, composed of lath-like\nplatelets. Four helically coiled brachioles arranged in\na 2-0-2 pattern in small juvenile specimens, to five in a 2-1-2\npattern in more mature juvenile specimens, to ten, each of the\nbrachiole bases splitting and essentially retaining the same\n2-1-2 pattern. Stalk sharply differentiated from thecal plates,\nthick, of variable length (30 to 50% thecal height), and composed\nof small circular to slightly faceted platelets. Attachment disc\nbroad and flattened.\n", "tree": "taxonomy"}
